# Citation metadata for GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and for Zenodo.
# Keep the authors, title and version in step with DESCRIPTION and inst/CITATION.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WildObsR, please cite it as below, and cite each data package you use."
type: software
title: "WildObsR: Discover, Access and Harmonise WildObs Camera Trap Data"
abstract: >-
  An R package to find, download and prepare camera trap data from WildObs, the
  Australian national wildlife camera database. Projects are downloaded as Camera
  Trap Data Packages (Camtrap DP) with their licences and citations, then harmonised
  to a shared spatial and temporal scale for occupancy and abundance models.
authors:
  - given-names: Zachary
    family-names: Amir
    email: z.amir@uq.edu.au
    affiliation: The University of Queensland
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8398-2059"
  - given-names: Tom
    family-names: Bruce
version: 0.3.0.9000
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/WildObs/WildObsR"
url: "https://github.com/WildObs/WildObsR"
keywords:
  - camera traps
  - Camtrap DP
  - biodiversity data
  - occupancy
  - R
